# media.kb — how information is published, carried and paid for, and how it goes wrong.
#
# `society.kb` has one line for journalism; `computing.kb` has the internet as plumbing — IP, DNS,
# HTTP — and nothing about what runs on it. So the whole vocabulary in which people discuss what
# they read and watch was absent: what an editor does, what a source is, what fake news is, what
# an algorithm feed does, what privacy means.
#
# This domain matters more than most for a system that will be asked about its own outputs. A
# brain that can generate text and holds no fact about misinformation can be part of the problem
# and cannot describe it.

# --- the press and its craft ------------------------------------------------------------------------ #
mass media | is_a=institution | means=the channels that carry information to a large audience | has_kind=newspaper | has_kind=radio | has_kind=television | has_kind=online media
news | is_a=information | means=an account of recent events thought to matter to an audience
newspaper | is_a=publication | purpose=reporting news in print on a regular schedule | has_part=headline | has_part=editorial | has_part=byline
headline | is_a=part of an article | purpose=telling the reader in a line what the piece is about | causes=most of what a passing reader takes away
byline | is_a=part of an article | means=the line naming who wrote it | purpose=attaching responsibility to a name
editorial | is_a=article | means=a piece stating the publication's own opinion | has_property=distinct from reporting
journalist | is_a=person | purpose=gathering, checking and writing news | requires=sources
editor | is_a=person | purpose=deciding what is published and in what form | capable_of=cutting, checking and rejecting a piece
source | is_a=person or document | means=where a journalist got the information | has_kind=primary source | has_kind=anonymous source
primary source | is_a=source | means=a record made by someone directly involved | has_property=stronger evidence than an account of an account
fact checking | is_a=process | purpose=verifying claims before or after publication | requires=going back to a primary source
correction | is_a=notice | purpose=setting right something a publication got wrong | causes=trust being maintained rather than lost
press freedom | is_a=right | means=the press being able to report without prior permission or reprisal | causes=power being reported on
censorship | is_a=practice | means=suppressing what may be published or said | causes=the public not knowing what was removed
libel | is_a=wrong | means=publishing a false statement that damages a reputation | causes=a claim for damages
plagiarism | is_a=wrong | means=passing off someone else's work as one's own | causes=loss of standing and of qualifications
attribution | is_a=practice | means=saying where a claim or a quotation came from | purpose=letting a reader check it
interview | is_a=method | means=getting information by asking a person directly
investigative journalism | is_a=journalism | means=reporting that uncovers what someone wanted hidden | requires=time and legal protection
propaganda | is_a=communication | means=material designed to promote a cause rather than to inform | has_property=may be true and still be propaganda
advertisement | is_a=communication | purpose=persuading an audience to buy or believe something | has_property=paid for by whoever benefits
public relations | is_a=activity | purpose=shaping how an organisation is seen

# --- broadcasting and publishing ------------------------------------------------------------------------ #
broadcasting | is_a=activity | means=sending the same content to many receivers at once | requires=a transmitter or a network
radio station | is_a=organisation | purpose=broadcasting sound programmes | requires=a frequency allocation
television channel | is_a=organisation | purpose=broadcasting picture and sound programmes
public broadcaster | is_a=organisation | purpose=broadcasting funded publicly rather than by advertising | requires=independence from the government of the day
streaming | is_a=technology | means=sending audio or video to be played as it arrives | requires=steady bandwidth | causes=viewing on demand rather than on a schedule
podcast | is_a=publication | means=an audio programme published for downloading or streaming
publishing | is_a=activity | means=making a work available to the public | has_kind=book publishing | has_kind=self publishing
edition | is_a=version | means=one issued form of a published work
circulation | is_a=measure | means=how many copies of a publication are distributed
audience | is_a=group | means=the people who receive a piece of communication
ratings | is_a=measure | means=an estimate of how many watched or listened | causes=what gets commissioned
paywall | is_a=mechanism | purpose=charging for access to content | causes=revenue not dependent on advertising

# --- the network and its platforms ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
social media | is_a=online media | means=platforms where users publish to each other | causes=anyone being able to reach an audience | causes=misinformation spreading as fast as news
platform | is_a=service | means=a service that hosts what other people make | has_property=usually not the author of what it carries
user generated content | is_a=content | means=material made by the audience rather than by a publisher
recommendation algorithm | is_a=algorithm | purpose=choosing what a user is shown next | causes=engagement being optimised rather than accuracy | causes=filter bubbles
filter bubble | is_a=phenomenon | means=seeing mostly what one already agrees with | occurs_when=a feed is tuned to what a user already clicked | causes=a distorted sense of what others think
echo chamber | is_a=phenomenon | means=a group in which the same view is repeated and rarely challenged | causes=beliefs hardening
viral content | is_a=content | means=material spreading rapidly by being shared | has_property=spread does not depend on being true
engagement | is_a=measure | means=how much an audience clicks, watches, comments or shares | causes=what a platform promotes
influencer | is_a=person | means=someone whose recommendations reach a large following
search engine | is_a=service | purpose=finding pages that answer a query | requires=an index of the web | causes=what most people ever see of the web
hyperlink | is_a=element | purpose=connecting one document to another | causes=the web being navigable
blog | is_a=publication | means=a site of dated entries by one author or a few
forum | is_a=service | purpose=discussion in threads on a topic
wiki | is_a=service | means=a site any reader may edit | requires=version history and review to stay reliable
open source | is_a=practice | means=publishing source code so anyone may read, use and change it | causes=review by people who did not write it
digital divide | is_a=problem | means=the gap between those with reliable network access and those without | causes=services moving online leaving people out

# --- truth, error and harm --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
misinformation | is_a=false information | means=false information spread without intent to deceive | causes=harm even where nobody meant it
disinformation | is_a=false information | means=false information spread deliberately to mislead | requires=intent
fake news | is_a=disinformation | means=fabricated material presented in the form of a news report
rumour | is_a=claim | means=a claim passed on without its source being checked | causes=panic when it concerns safety
conspiracy theory | is_a=belief | means=explaining events as the secret work of a powerful group | has_property=treats absence of evidence as evidence of concealment
clickbait | is_a=technique | means=a headline written to be clicked rather than to describe | causes=disappointment and distrust
deepfake | is_a=synthetic media | means=a convincing fabricated image, video or voice | requires=machine learning | causes=recordings no longer being self-evidently evidence
media literacy | is_a=skill | means=being able to judge who made a piece of media, why, and how well it is evidenced | purpose=not being misled | requires=checking the source
lateral reading | is_a=technique | means=leaving a page to find out who is behind it before judging its claims | causes=faster and better assessment than reading it closely
primary evidence | is_a=evidence | purpose=checking a claim against the record rather than against another report
bias in reporting | is_a=problem | means=a slant in what is selected and how it is framed | has_property=present in selection as well as in wording
false balance | is_a=problem | means=presenting two sides as equal when the evidence is not | causes=a settled question looking open

# --- privacy and data ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ #
privacy | is_a=right | means=control over what is known about oneself and by whom | causes=a limit on what may be collected
personal data | is_a=information | means=information about an identified or identifiable person | requires=protection by law in many countries
data protection | is_a=practice | purpose=keeping personal data safe and used only as agreed
consent | is_a=permission | means=agreement freely given after being told what it is for | requires=being informed to be real
surveillance | is_a=practice | means=systematic watching of people | causes=a chilling effect on what people say and do
tracking | is_a=practice | means=following what a person does across sites or places | requires=identifiers such as cookies
cookie | is_a=file | purpose=letting a site remember a visitor between requests | causes=tracking when shared across sites
anonymisation | is_a=technique | purpose=removing what would identify a person from a data set | has_property=harder than it looks, since records can be re-linked
encryption in transit | is_a=technique | purpose=stopping anyone between two parties from reading what passes
phishing | is_a=attack | means=a message pretending to be from someone trusted to obtain credentials | causes=account takeover | requires=the target acting on it
password | is_a=credential | purpose=proving who is asking | requires=being unique to each service to be worth much
two factor authentication | is_a=technique | means=requiring a second proof besides a password | causes=a stolen password no longer being enough
malware | is_a=software | means=software written to damage or intrude | has_kind=virus | has_kind=ransomware | has_kind=spyware
ransomware | is_a=malware | means=software that encrypts a victim's files and demands payment | requires=backups to recover from without paying
backup | is_a=copy | purpose=being able to restore data after loss | requires=being kept somewhere the original problem cannot reach
cyber security | is_a=discipline | purpose=protecting systems and data from attack | involves=access control | involves=patching known flaws
digital footprint | is_a=record | means=the trail a person's online activity leaves behind | has_property=hard to remove once it is copied
